          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The main upside risk is a renewed fuel or housing-related acceleration that would land above the interval, especially at 4.6% or higher. The main downside risk is another large favorable volatile-item or base-effect move, with a result at or below 3.2% landing outside the interval."
