          "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior starts from May DSPI 23651.7 plus the Feb 2024-May 2026 base-rate sample of 28 monthly changes with mean change +77.5. I adjust down by about 19.2 billion for likely fading of May's farm-proprietor boost and tax drag, giving a point change of +58.3 and point level 23651.7 + 58.3 = 23710.0. For realized dispersion, successive changes from Feb 2024-May 2026 sum to 2170.8 over 28 changes, mean = 77.5, sum of squared deviations = 145189.3 over 27 df, so sigma = sqrt(145189.3/27) = 73.3; the normal 80 percent half-width is about 1.28*sigma = 93.8. The ladder-implied half-width is (23840.0 - 23620.0)/2 = 110.0, or 1.17x the sigma half-width, widened modestly because farm-payment and tax timing can dominate one month of DPI."
