          "text": "Prior/update/interval: use a level-persistence model anchored at the fetched May value of 23651.7 and the four-change January-May 2026 reference class (-13.5, +128.0, -23.5, +164.8). The mean-change prior is +63.95 billion; with no quantitatively supported new June adjustment, the central level is about 23715.7 before ladder interpolation. The sample standard deviation is sqrt(27920.3/3) = 96.5 billion. A normal-reference 80% range is approximately 63.95 +/- 1.282*96.5, or changes of -59.8 to +187.7 billion, corresponding to levels near 23591.9 to 23839.4. The elicited ladder rounds and slightly discretizes that calculation, giving final implied bounds of 23590.0 to 23836.7."
