          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Upside risk is unusually large benefit, interest, refund, or agency-payment timing that lifts the deficit above $350 billion. Downside risk is unusually strong receipts or delayed outlays that reduce it below $190 billion. An exceptional payment-timing or receipt event would land outside the interval."
